Z||000009||Shaft||12-30-2000||12:39 AM||||My favorite Mario Stat:<P>He has 3 games in which he scored 5 goals. One of those games he scord a goal every way possible. (Even Strength, Shorthanded, Power Play, Empty Net)<P>As for the long term effects of a player/owner on the ice:<P>This has been addressed by many sports casters and I don't think it will really have a great effect. Mario is unlike any other owner and has been in the locker room for every game. He even spoke to the team after every game. Most of the guys on the team have either played with Mario or looked up to him at some point in their career, and they seemed to be joking around with him on the bench. The other players have accepted him because of his ability and they feel they can win more games with him. And since he's on the ice now he does not have voting rights in the NHL anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000010||kslish||12-30-2000||03:55 PM||||Game 2 of the comeback is tonight......<P>If he keeps this level of play up, I'm getting playoff tickets.<P>What I found even more impressive to his personal performance is how Mario being on the ice elevates Jagr's gameplay to the next level by diverting some attention from him. It's truely amazing watching the two best players in hockey right now complement each other.  It's almost as if they know what the other one is thinking on the ice at the same time.<P>As for Gretzky....will see how the numbers fall in a few more years. <P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT<BR>Pittsburgh, PA||||reg||14
